// A queue monitor projected to sound, declaring one status: muted.
//
// Silence is the CORRECT rendering of "waiting, inactive" -- an earcon
// announcing inactivity is a contradiction, and the sound plane found that by
// building it. So the defect is not the muted. The defect is that muted is the
// ONLY status this surface declares, on a channel that renders it as nothing:
// the surface promises the operator a perceptible status and emits silence,
// forever. Imperceivable state in the declared medium -- Rule 82.
//
// Needs both axes to see: the signal vocabulary and the medium enumeration.
//
// Expected: SIGNAL_UNPERCEIVABLE

DEFINE VIBE queue_audio (
  SURFACE_AS auditory
)

DEFINE SCREEN queue_monitor (
  SATISFIES [DISCOVER, UNDERSTAND],
  SIGNALS [muted]
)
